U|                         If only she was ordinary.
O|
N|               Stella sprinkles powder on his back, spreads it around.
O|
N,G|               THE CAMERA PULLS BACK as she helps Jeff to a sitting position. 
N|               He buttons on his shirt.
O|
C|                                     STELLA
U|                         You're never going to marry?
O|
C|                                     JEFF
U|                         Probably. But when I do, it'll be to 
U|                         someone who thinks of life as more 
U|                         than a new dress, a lobster dinner, 
U|                         and the latest scandal. I need a 
U|                         woman who'll go anywhere, do anything, 
U|                         and love it.
O|
N,G|               THE CAMERA MOVES IN as she helps him into the wheelchair, 
N|               listening to him with exaggerated attention. He, stops as he 
N|               notice her attitude. Then he goes on with less conviction:
O|
C|                                     JEFF
U|                         The only honest thing to do is call 
U|                         it off. Let her look for somebody 
U|                         else.
O|
C|                                     STELLA
