N|               Stella leaves for the kitchen in a huff. Jeff turns his chair 
N|               to the window.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - DAY - SEMI-CLOSEUP
O|
N|               Jeff now looks out to see what has happened to the old lady, 
N|               and the man with the flowers.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - DAY - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               The elderly lady is now asleep in her deck chair, her face 
N|               covered with the Herald Tribune. There is no sign of the man 
N|               with the flowers.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - DAY - CLOSEUP
O|
N|               Jeff's eyes travel up to the ballet dancer's window.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - DAY - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               She is sitting near the window looking into an upright mirror. 
N|               Dreamily, and methodically, she is brushing her long copper-
N|               colored hair.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - DAY - CLOSEUP
O|
N|               His eyes are suddenly turned in another direction, sharply 
N|               to his left.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - DAY - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               He is now looking at the windows of the apartments nearest 
N|               to him. A shade has gone up, and a man, obviously a caretaker 
N|               is raising a window with some effort. Having accomplished 
N,G|               this, he turns back into the room, and we now see him approach 
N|               a young man and woman who are standing just inside the 
N|               doorway. He hands a key to the young man, and then obligingly 
N|               brings in two suitcases which he places on the floor beside 
N|               them. He gives them a studied, but agreeable nod, then 
N|               departs.
O|
N,G|               We now see that the girl has a small hat with a veil, and an 
N|               ornate corsage pinned to her light blue tailored suit. The 
N|               boy, who like the girl is perhaps twenty years old, wears a 
N|               dark blue serge suit and a grey felt hat. He takes off the 
N|               hat, and scales it over to a nearby chair. Quickly they are 
N|               in each other's arms, kissing passionately, crushing the 
N|               girl's corsage and pushing her hat back a little. They part, 
N|               the boy laughs nervously, and takes a furtive glance out 
N|               toward the corridor. He looks back into the room, and beckons 
N|               her to come out. She follows him wonderingly. For a moment, 
N|               both are lost from sight. When they reappear, he is carrying 
N|               her in his arms, over the threshold. He sets her down, closes 
N|               the door, and they kiss again.
O|
N|               They part, still holding hands and looking into each other's 
N|               eyes. Then slowly, and significantly, she looks toward the 
N|               open window. He releases her hands, goes to the window and 
N|               pull down the shade, as she is reaching upward with both 
N|               hands to unpin her hat.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - DAY - SEMI-CLOSEUP
O|
N|               There is a soft, understanding look on Jeff's face, and he 
N|               gives an involuntary sigh. He is unaware that Stella is now 
N|               standing behind him.
O|
C|                                     STELLA
P|                              (Quietly)
U|                         Window shopper.
O|
N|               He freezes, turns slowly to look up at her.
O|
