O|
N|               Jeff gives a sigh of relief, exhaling his breath, then looks 
N|               down toward his legs in thought. He holds this attitude for 
N|               just a moment, then seems to shake off his concern to lift 
N|               his head and turn his attention to what might be happening 
N|               in his neighborhood beyond his window.
O|
N|               Behind him we see the vague form of Lisa bringing in a card 
N|               table, which she proceeds to unfold.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - NIGHT - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               Jeff's attention is concentrated on an apartment we have not 
N|               seen before. This belongs to a single woman, about forty 
N|               years of age. She lives alone. Her apartment is below that 
N|               of the salesman with the invalid wife.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - NIGHT - CLOSEUP
O|
N|               Jeff leans forward with increased interest. Behind him we 
N|               get vague figure of Lisa laying a cloth over the card table.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - NIGHT - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               A nearer view show us a more intimate picture of the woman 
N|               Jeff is concentrating on. She is thin and unattractive. At 
N|               the moment, she is putting on her make-up in front of the 
N|               bedroom mirror. She gives a half turn and picks up a pair of 
N|               horn-rimmed glasses, which she puts on, and leans nearer to 
N|               her mirror. She picks up a lipstick and proceeds to paint 
N|               her lips carefully.
O|
N|               Having completed her make-up, she takes off her glasses and 
N|               surveys her face in the mirror. She stands up, swings the 
N|               skirt of her dress around, admires herself in the mirror. 
N|               She is quite flat-chested, and the dress hangs unattractively. 
N|               She lifts her chin, gives one last look, and turns toward 
N|               her living room. As if she's preparing to meet someone.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - NIGHT - CLOSEUP
O|
N|               Without taking his eyes from the scene, Jeff picks up his 
N|               wineglass and drinks. As he drinks, his eyes move slightly 
N|               over.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD NIGHT - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N,G|               THE CAMERA HAS PANNED slightly to the woman's living room 
N|               window. A small, candle-lit table is set up, with dinner for 
N|               two. The spinster sweeps into the room, smiling. She goes to 
N|               the door, opens it, and in pantomime admits an imaginary 
N|               caller. She pretends to kiss him lightly, take his hat, and 
N|               place the hat on a chair. Then she shows him to a seat at 
N|               the table, disappears into an unseen kitchen and returns 
N|               with a bottle and two glasses. She sits down, pours two 
N|               drinks. She lifts her drink in a toast to the imaginary man 
N|               opposite her.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - NIGHT - CLOSEUP
O|
N|               Jeff gives a faint, sympathetic smile, and subconsciously 
N|               raises his glass in response. In the background, Lisa, having 
N|               just placed a pair of candlesticks on the table, is returning 
N|               to the kitchen.
O|
S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD - NIGHT - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               Having finished her drink, the lonesome woman pours herself 
N|               another one. Then she starts to take a sip, smiling across 
N|               the table at her imaginary guest. She lowers the glass onto 
N|               the table. The smile fades from her face as her head drops. 
N|               Suddenly she buries her head in her arms over the table and 
N|               starts to sob.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - NIGHT - SEMI-CLOSEUP
O|
