S,G|               EXT. NEIGHBORHOOD NIGHT - SEMI-LONG SHOT
O|
N|               The kitchen-lining room combination of the ballet dancer's 
N|               apartment has now been made more presentable.
O|
N|               The ice box is now skillfully concealed by a large Chinese 
N|               screen. All kitchen utensils have been put away, replaced by 
N|               more attractive effects, and lamp light softens the 
N|               surroundings.
O|
N|               Miss Torso is now wearing a cocktail dress, which shows off 
N|               her figure to great advantage, especially when she leans 
N|               toward three assorted men to offer them a plate of hors d' 
N|               oeuvres. She is the perfect hostess, animated, charming, and 
N|               with an added personal touch for each guest. She is behaving 
N|               with a sophistication which was not apparent when we first 
N|               saw her in the morning. Her every movement is followed 
N|               admiringly by the eyes of the three men -- one wearing black 
N|               tie, with a touch of grey in his hair, a Long Island socialite -- 
N|               a young rather handsome, actor in grey flannel suit -- and 
N|               last, a bright, pleasant, young man who might possibly be 
N|               from Wall street, wearing a blue-pin-striped suit. The latter 
N|               two are engaged in an animated conversation. The young man 
N|               in the grey suit is showing the other young man some newspaper 
N|               cuttings he's taken from his pocket.
O|
N|               Miss Torso sees that the cocktail glass of the third man is 
N|               empty. She takes it over to the window, and starts to fill 
N|               it. The man in the tuxedo follows her over, with a casual 
N|               glance toward the other two. He stands beside her as she 
N|               makes the drink. He looks at his watch with some impatience, 
N|               and makes a side comment to her as to the lateness of the 
N|               time. She turns, gives him a light kiss on his cheek, as if 
N|               she's telling him to be patient. Instead of pacifying him, 
N|               it makes him more amorous, and he puts an arm around her 
N|               shoulder an plants a heavy kiss on her cheek. She turns to 
N|               face him, they look into each other's eyes a moment, and she 
N|               allows herself to be kissed on the lips -- but only long 
N|               enough so as to attract the attention of the other two men. 
N|               With a little admonishing look, she moves away from him, and 
N|               makes him rejoin the other two.
O|
S,G|               INT. JEFF'S APARTMENT - NIGHT - SEMI-CLOSEUP
O|
